Feature: Briefing emails are sent once, and only inside the allowed date window

  # BL-821. Two independent legs. Leg A: a successful send persists .sent.json
  # to the shared durable store, so a pull, a second host, or a fresh worktree
  # cannot re-mail history. Leg B: the ordinary sweep only mails briefings dated
  # today or yesterday (UTC), so a stale marker cannot dump the archive. A
  # briefing suppressed by the window is reported, never silently skipped.
  #
  # PARKED AS .feature.draft per BL-233: this slice is not built, so a live
  # *.feature here would have no step handlers and would hard-fail the
  # acceptance runner for every other ticket. The coder renames this to
  # .feature and lands its step handlers in the same parcel.

  Background:
    Given a briefings directory and a sent-marker the sweep reads

  # BL-821 successful-send-persists-marker-durably-01
  Scenario: a successful send persists the marker to the durable store
    Given an unsent briefing dated today
    When the sweep mails it successfully
    Then the briefing is recorded as sent in the durable store
    And a fresh checkout of that store already lists it as sent

  # BL-821 failed-send-does-not-mark-sent-02
  Scenario: a failed send leaves the briefing unsent
    Given an unsent briefing dated today
    When the sweep tries to mail it and the send fails
    Then the briefing is not recorded as sent in the durable store
    And the next sweep tries it again

  # BL-821 stale-marker-does-not-remail-archive-03
  Scenario: a checkout with a stale marker does not re-mail the archive
    Given a checkout whose marker is missing every briefing older than yesterday
    And those older briefing files are present on disk
    When the sweep runs
    Then none of those older briefings is mailed

  # BL-821 window-admits-today-and-yesterday-04
  Scenario Outline: only briefings dated today or yesterday are mailed
    Given an unsent briefing dated <briefing date>
    When the sweep runs
    Then the briefing is <disposition>

    Examples:
      | briefing date       | disposition |
      | today               | mailed      |
      | yesterday           | mailed      |
      | two days ago        | suppressed  |
      | a month ago         | suppressed  |

  # BL-821 window-is-utc-05
  Scenario: the window is evaluated in UTC, not host local time
    Given a host whose local date differs from the UTC date
    And an unsent briefing dated today in UTC
    When the sweep runs
    Then the briefing is mailed
    And the window decision used the UTC date

  # BL-821 suppressed-briefing-is-reported-06
  Scenario: a briefing held back by the window says so
    Given an unsent briefing dated two days ago
    When the sweep runs
    Then the sweep reports that briefing as suppressed for being outside the window
    And that report is distinguishable from having generated no briefing at all

  # BL-821 mailed-once-across-hosts-07
  Scenario: two hosts sharing the durable store mail a briefing once
    Given two hosts running the sweep against the same durable store
    And an unsent briefing dated today
    When both hosts run their sweep
    Then the briefing is mailed exactly once

  # BL-821 marker-commit-carries-only-the-marker-08
  Scenario: persisting the marker does not carry unrelated changes
    Given unrelated modified files in the working tree
    And an unsent briefing dated today
    When the sweep mails it successfully
    Then only the marker is committed to the durable store
    And the unrelated modified files remain uncommitted

  # BL-821 non-dated-briefing-name-decided-deliberately-09
  Scenario: a briefing whose name is not a plain date is decided, not crashed on
    Given an unsent briefing file whose name carries a suffix beyond the date
    When the sweep runs
    Then the window predicate reaches a definite decision for that file
    And the sweep does not fail

  # BL-821 no-unbounded-catchup-without-operator-action-10
  Scenario: the ordinary sweep never performs unbounded catch-up
    Given a marker listing nothing at all
    And a long history of briefing files on disk
    When the sweep runs
    Then only briefings inside the window are mailed
    And mailing the rest requires an explicit one-shot operator action
